      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Google as Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google as the initial external provider for this OAuth/OIDC login flow. I'm focusing on creating the `start_oauth_login.py` script now, and this choice gives me a well-documented starting point.\n\n\n**Constructing Authorization URL**\n\nI'm now fully immersed in building `start_oauth_login.py`. I've outlined the necessary components: the Google OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint and the key parameters such as client ID, redirect URI, scope, and response type. I intend to hardcode these values as placeholders for now, anticipating their eventual sourcing from environment variables or a configuration file. The code will generate the authorization URL for redirection.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866918323,
          "start": 1789866915990
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc61b896001LT05F21ZmSLtdf",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc61b35000173mPJ5egI6ZBfw",
      "session_id": "ses_f439e4d37ffePU1rMcxNECltdT",
      "time_created": 1789866915990,
      "time_updated": 1789866918323
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "g5x5syBZ4XAMI6gf",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "\nimport os\nimport urllib.parse\n\n# Google OAuth 2.0 Authorization Endpoint\nGOOGLE_AUTHORIZATION_BASE_URL = \"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth\"\n\n# Client ID and Redirect URI (these would typically be loaded from environment variables or a config file)\nCLIENT_ID = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\", \"YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\")\nREDIRECT_URI = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI\", \"http://localhost:8000/oauth_callback\")\nSCOPE = \"openid profile email\"  # OIDC scopes\nRESPONSE_TYPE = \"code\"\n\ndef start_oauth_login():\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs the Google OAuth 2.0 authorization URL and returns it.\n    In a real application, you would redirect the user to this URL.\n    \"\"\"\n    params = {\n        \"client_id\": CLIENT_ID,\n        \"redirect_uri\": REDIRECT_URI,\n        \"scope\": SCOPE,\n        \"response_type\": RESPONSE_TYPE,\n        \"access_type\": \"offline\",  # Request a refresh token\n        \"prompt\": \"consent\",       # Force consent screen\n    }\n    authorization_url = f\"{GOOGLE_AUTHORIZATION_BASE_URL}?{urllib.parse.urlencode(params)}\"\n    return authorization_url\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    login_url = start_oauth_login()\n    print(f\"Please visit this URL to start the OAuth login process:\\n{login_url}\")\n",
